From cc65c0234ce6d1591cd6f5670e139aa722109aaa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 16:19:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/11] Bugfix: make error handling of `dgraphCoarsenBuild()`
 collective [report R. Perry]

A process that could not allocate its thread work array, its coarse
graph arrays in non-debug builds, or its adjacency hash table returned
alone from `dgraphCoarsenBuild()`, while the other processes entered
the multinode exchange, the adjacency exchange or the final reduction
and waited forever.

Allocate the thread work array in `dgraphCoarsenInit()`, along with
the other data that lives until `dgraphCoarsenExit()`, so that its
failure is agreed upon with the ones of the other initial allocations.
Always perform the agreement on the allocation of the coarse graph
arrays, as in `hdgraphGather()`. Carry the result of the adjacency
computation in the final reduction, as `dgraphGhst()` does, so that
all processes free the coarse graph together, and shrink the edge
arrays only once the coarse graph is known to be valid everywhere.

Refs: DGR-13
